# Backend Restoration Walkthrough

The backend was previously non-functional due to a missing model file ([models/grade.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/models/grade.py)) which caused a `ModuleNotFoundError` during startup. This has been resolved, and the server is now fully operational.

## Changes Made

### 1. Restored Missing Models
Recreated [backend/models/grade.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/models/grade.py) with the following `SQLModel` definitions:
- [GradeComponent](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/models/grade.py#5-14): Tracks course-level grade categories (e.g., Finals, Midterms).
- [GradeEntry](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/models/grade.py#15-22): Stores individual user scores for components.

### 2. Updated Router Imports
Modified [backend/routers/brief.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/routers/brief.py) to correctly import and use the restored [GradeComponent](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/models/grade.py#5-14) and [GradeEntry](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/models/grade.py#15-22) models.

### 3. Server Restoration
- Identified and terminated stalled processes on port 8000.
- Restarted the backend using the local virtual environment.
- Verified database initialization and scheduler job registration.

